{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["And it is juxtaposed to <b>you shall not commit adultery</b> — to murder, as written: רצוח וגנוב ונאוף (murder, and steal, and commit adultery). And likewise one who emits seed לבטלה (in vain) is as if he commits all three. And here it is written ולא תנאף with a superfluous vav, corresponding to six times מאררים (those who curse). And this is the explanation of Miriam, as written in the chapter of Sotah. And it is juxtaposed to it: ולא תגנוב (and you shall not steal) — because of מים גנובים ימתקו (stolen waters are sweet). And it is written כן עוד with a superfluous vav, corresponding to six things written at the beginning of Proverbs: נארבה לדם נצפנה לנקי חנם (let us lurk for blood, let us ambush the innocent without cause), etc. And it is juxtaposed to it: ולא תענה ברעך עדות שקר (and you shall not bear false witness against your fellow) — for one who steals testifies false testimony about himself, for he causes himself to be sold as a slave. And He added in it a vav: by his testimony the world is afflicted — for it was created in six days."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The phrase 'וז\"פ מרים' is obscure; translated hyper-literally. 'ש\"ז' expanded as שז\"ל with elided vav; 'לוקה' read as לוקה (is afflicted/stricken). The six verses from Proverbs 1:11–14 are abbreviated by their opening words."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:58.940692853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}